// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The prior strategy opened << almost immediately based on punctuation cues like "=",
// which caused constrained mode to start too early and then remain unterminated.
// This revision makes constrained spans conservative and self-closing:
//
// 1. Outside constrained mode, generation stays unconstrained by default.
// 2. A constrained span is opened only after some substantial free-form text has
//    already been produced beyond the incoming generatedPrefix, reducing the chance
//    of entering << at the start of the continuation.
// 3. A span is opened only when there is enough remaining budget to both write at
//    least one constrained token and then close with >>.
// 4. Once inside constrained mode, the strategy prioritizes closing as soon as the
